---
description: Tailwind-on-tags, no legacy CSS classes, copy colocated with components
globs: frontend/**/*.{tsx,ts,jsx,css}
alwaysApply: true
---

# Frontend styling & copy

Applies to the entire frontend source. Put styles on elements with **standard Tailwind utilities**. Do not invent named classes in `globals.css` when utilities already cover the look.

## Color palette

Semantic colors live in `frontend/app/globals.css` `@theme` and map to Tailwind default scales. Prefer these over raw `neutral-*` / `rose-*`:

| Token | Role | Tailwind source |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `canvas` | Page background | `neutral-950` |
| `surface` | Cards / panels | `neutral-900` |
| `elevated` / `elevated-hover` | Raised panels | `neutral-800` / `700` |
| `foreground` | Primary text on dark | `neutral-50` |
| `muted` / `subtle` | Secondary text | `neutral-400` / `500` |
| `accent` / `accent-soft` / `accent-strong` / `accent-deep` | Brand rose | `rose-400` … `600` |
| `accent-ink` / `paper-accent` | Rose on light | `rose-800` |
| `secondary` | Warm highlight | `amber-200` |
| `paper` / `paper-foreground` | Light sections | `stone-100` / `neutral-950` |
| `success` | Positive / lime callouts | `lime-300` |
| `ring` | Focus rings | `rose-400` |

Examples: `bg-canvas`, `text-accent`, `bg-paper`, `ring-ring`, `from-accent-soft to-secondary`.

## Do

1. Write `className` on the tag with Tailwind utilities (`flex`, `rounded-3xl`, `bg-canvas`, `lg:grid-cols-4`, …).
2. Use **default breakpoints only**: `sm`, `md`, `lg`, `xl`, `2xl` (and their `max-*` forms). Never `max-[850px]`, `min-[540px]`, etc.
3. Prefer default scale tokens (`text-sm`, `p-6`, `rounded-3xl`, `max-w-6xl`, `gap-4`) over arbitrary values (`p-[26px]`, `max-w-[365px]`, `tracking-[0.22em]`).
4. For hover overlays / gradients / badges / “soon” labels, use real child elements — not custom `::before` / `::after` CSS classes.
5. Drive scrolled/open/active UI state with conditional `className` in React, not `[data-*]` or bare `is-*` CSS hooks.
6. When migrating a surface, remove its unused named classes from `globals.css`.

## Don't

- Add new `.site-*`, `.drama-*`, `.btn-*`, `.studio-*`, or similar component classes to `globals.css`
- Keep or introduce legacy CSS classNames on components (`studio-modal`, `is-active` via CSS, …)
- Use arbitrary breakpoints (`max-[850px]`, `min-[1100px]`, …)
- Keep a custom class that only `@apply`s a utility string — put those utilities on the tag instead
- Invent new hex colors in JSX when a palette or Tailwind scale token fits

## Copy and hardcoded data

1. User-facing strings, filter lists, error maps, and static chips live in a local `copy/` (or `data/`) module next to the feature — e.g. `components/<feature>/copy/*.ts` or `(pages)/<route>/data/*.ts`.
2. One concern per module. Components import copy; only dynamic interpolations stay inline.
3. Do not leave long hardcode lists or UI copy strings inside JSX/components.

## Exceptions

- Global base resets (`a { text-decoration }`, fonts / palette via `@theme`) may stay in CSS
- Rare one-off values may use a single arbitrary utility on the element — still no named CSS class for it
- Existing leftover named CSS may remain only until that surface is migrated; new and touched UI must be Tailwind-on-tags

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — legacy CSS class
<section className="studio-modal">…</section>

// ✅ GOOD — Tailwind on the tag
<section className="relative w-full max-w-md rounded-2xl bg-elevated p-8 text-foreground">…</section>
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — inline hardcode
<button>Create from scratch</button>

// ✅ GOOD — from a local copy module
import { featureCopy } from "./copy/feature";
<button>{featureCopy.createFromScratch}</button>
```
